# Hexagonal Architecture

## Layer dependency order

```
domain ← application ← infrastructure / interfaces
```

`domain` — pure Python: entities, exceptions, async `Protocol` ports.
No FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Pydantic, httpx.

`application` — use cases and optional DTOs when the result differs from a domain entity.
Imports `domain` (and its own packages). No infrastructure, interfaces, or frameworks.

`infrastructure` — implements outbound ports (SQLAlchemy, httpx, …).

`interfaces` — inbound adapters. FastAPI routers and Pydantic HTTP schemas.
Calls use cases only. Maps domain results to HTTP. No SQL, no business rules.

`main.py` — composition root. The only module that imports both
`infrastructure` and `interfaces`.

## Ports

Define ports as `typing.Protocol` in `domain/ports/`.
Methods are `async def`.
Name ports after their role: `NoteRepository`, `EmailSender`, `PaymentGateway`.

## Use cases

One class per use case: `GetNoteById`, `CreateUser`, `CancelOrder`.
Constructor receives ports via dependency injection (plain `__init__`, not FastAPI `Depends`).
Single public method: `async def execute(...)`.

## HTTP schemas

Pydantic v2 models live in `interfaces/api/schemas/`.
Do not use domain dataclasses as FastAPI `response_model`.

## No cross-layer imports

```python
# BAD — infrastructure in domain
from sqlalchemy.orm import Session  # inside domain/

# BAD — adapter in interfaces
from app.infrastructure.persistence.tables import NoteTable  # inside interfaces/

# GOOD
from app.domain.ports.note_repository import NoteRepository  # in application/
```

Wire adapters in `main.py` and pass use cases into `build_*_router(...)`.
